entries.description:
Since Δ = p(p + 4):
p < −4 gives Δ > 0, so there are two intercepts;
−4 < p < 0 gives Δ < 0, so there are no intercepts;
p > 0 gives Δ > 0, so there are two intercepts.
At the boundary values p = −4 and p = 0, there is one intercept.

The parabola opens upwards. Therefore:
m < 0 gives minimum value −2m > 0, so there are no intercepts;
m = 0 gives minimum value 0, so there is one intercept;
m > 0 gives minimum value −2m < 0, so there are two intercepts.

A parabola:
• passes through the origin;
• has two x-intercepts that are 4 units apart;
• has its vertex on the line y = x − 6.
Find every possible equation of the parabola.
